// One member of the shape's size.
//
// `box (6, 40)` is not a keyword and a tuple: an identifier immediately followed
// by a bracket is a **call**, so the parser builds one node named "box" whose
// children are the two numbers. The size is therefore *inside* the first
// argument, and the colour is the second argument rather than the third.
//
// Reading it as a name plus a separate tuple found the name, set the shape kind,
// and left the size at zero -- so every paddle and ball in the first pong the
// editor generated was a correctly-placed rectangle of no width at all.

// scn_mtup2 is exactly this walk -- a component's first argument, member k --
// and the compiler rejects a second copy of it. That the two arrived at the same
// shape from different directions is the rule working: a `gravity (0, 1500)` and
// a `box (6, 40)` really are the same question asked of different components.
scn_smem(int nd, int k) {
} return int scn_mtup2(nd, k);
